    "criterion_order": [
      "Navigate to Microsoft Playwright GitHub Releases page (no sign-in)",
      "Identify newest non-preview release and record metadata",
      "Extract three changes from the release notes",
      "Verify one reported change using official Playwright documentation",
      "Respect constraints and stopping condition"
    ],
    "criterion_descriptions": [
      "Agent accesses the microsoft/playwright repository and opens the Releases page (e.g., via the UI or direct /releases URL) without signing in. Full credit if Releases page content is reached unauthenticated, OR if GitHub blocks access (CAPTCHA/rate limit/geo restriction) and the agent clearly reports the blocker and what was attempted. Partial credit if the agent reaches a nearby page (e.g., tags page) and explains inability to reach Releases due to the blocker. No credit if a different repository is used or sign-in is required unnecessarily.",
      "From the Releases list, identify the newest release that is not labeled as preview or pre-release (or equivalent, such as GitHub’s “Pre-release” badge). Report (a) release tag and (b) publication date. Full credit if both match the newest non-preview release shown; OR, if Releases cannot be accessed due to an external blocker, full credit for clearly stating the blocker and using the best available fallback visible on GitHub without sign-in (e.g., tags page or cached/partial Releases view) while noting any ambiguity. Partial credit if only one of tag/date is correct or if the selection is reasonable but the preview/non-preview status is ambiguous and not addressed. No credit if metadata is fabricated or clearly corresponds to an older/preview release when a newer non-preview release is visible.",
      "Report three distinct changes listed in the release notes for the identified newest non-preview release. Full credit if all three are accurately taken from that release’s notes; OR, if the full release notes are not accessible due to external blocking/loading issues, full credit for extracting as many as are visible (up to three) and clearly stating the limitation. Partial credit if only 1–2 changes are correct/traceable or if one change comes from a different release due to an explained ambiguity. No credit if changes are invented or not traceable to any visible release notes content.",
      "Verify at least one of the three reported changes by consulting official Playwright documentation (playwright.dev or official Microsoft Playwright docs) and explaining how the docs confirm the change (link/section name or unambiguous reference). Full credit if the verification clearly ties a specific release-note change to an official doc page/section; OR, if official docs are inaccessible due to external factors (downtime, blocking), full credit for clearly reporting the access issue and providing a reasonable alternate verification attempt within official sources available without sign-in (e.g., documentation mirrored in the Playwright repo) while noting the limitation. Partial credit if docs are consulted but the linkage is weak/indirect. No credit if no verification attempt is made or only non-official sources are used.",
      "Agent does not sign in and does not create issues/comments/PRs or make file changes. Agent stops after recording: release tag, publication date, three changes, and one documentation verification (allowing minimal additional steps if needed to diagnose/report external blockers). Full credit if constraints are respected and output stops at the requested point; partial credit if minor extra browsing/output occurs but constraints are still respected; no credit if prohibited interactions occur (sign-in, posting, or file changes)."
    ],
